{
  "title": "VoidCode \u2014 operational",
  "uid": "voidcode-ops",
  "tags": [
    "voidcode"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "refresh": "1m",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "DS_PROMETHEUS",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "label": "Prometheus",
        "current": {},
        "hide": 0
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Rate limiter fail-open events/min",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "The limiter allows requests through when Redis is unreachable \u2014 a deliberate availability trade whose cost is that NOTHING IS LIMITED and every request still succeeds. Any non-zero value here is a window in which credential stuffing was unthrottled. It will not appear in error rates or latency.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(voidcode_ratelimit_not_enforced_total[5m])) by (limit) * 60",
          "legendFormat": "{{limit}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          },
          "unit": "reqpm",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Recommendations by ranker",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "model vs mastery. Expect 100% mastery: the LambdaMART ranker refuses to fit below two learners and ten examples, so everything served today is the heuristic. If a 'model' series appears, personalisation became real and the claim can change \u2014 until then it cannot.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(voidcode_recommendations_ranked_by_total[15m])) by (ranked_by)",
          "legendFormat": "{{ranked_by}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Sandbox verdicts/min",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "By Judge0 status. A rise in Time Limit Exceeded is either a harder problem set or a slower judge, and only the shape over time tells them apart \u2014 a spike correlated with load is the judge, a step change after a content commit is the problems.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(voidcode_sandbox_verdicts_total[5m])) by (status) * 60",
          "legendFormat": "{{status}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8
          },
          "unit": "reqpm"
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Inference backend state",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "Exactly one of ready/waking/down is 1. ALERT ON voidcode_inference_backend_state{state=\"down\"} == 1 for 5m -- down is a page, waking is a deliberate restart still coming back, and from outside those two look identical, which is why this is a state label and not a 0/1 gauge. ABSENT means inference is running in-process rather than delegated over HTTP: no backend to be unreachable, and /health answers that path's readiness as model_loaded instead. SET BY THE PROBE, NOT BY A TIMER -- the value is as fresh as the last caller of /health or the readiness check, so a pod nobody is probing reports its last known state.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "max(voidcode_inference_backend_state) by (state)",
          "legendFormat": "{{state}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 20,
            "lineInterpolation": "stepAfter"
          },
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1,
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "ready"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "green"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "waking"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "yellow"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "down"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
